    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297-a1">

                <pb facs="0779" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg657"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 82.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prince Devawongse
                            Varoprakar to Mr. Child.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: Referring to previous
                    correspondence regarding the establishment of a hospital by the American
                    Presbyterian Mission in Ratburi, I have the honor to inform you that His Majesty
                    has been graciously pleased to grant the use of a government house to Dr. Hays
                    and Dr. Thompson for that purpose, and that an agreement has been signed.</p>
                <p>I have handed the official letter of the Kralahorne department to Phya
                    Anarien-tharuchai, governor of Ratburi, to Dr. Hays and Dr. Thompson, so that
                    they may take possession of the house.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Devawongse
                    Varoprakar.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
